      "Kwame Osei had taken Baikonur with four hundred men and eleven trucks, and he had done it on a Tuesday, and by Friday the price of a seat to orbit had a number attached to it that anyone could look up.",
      "That was the part that frightened the world. Not the violence — there had been violence before, in Jakarta, in Lagos, over the water in the Sahel. The frightening part was the *pricing*. Kwame had put launch capacity on a market with published rates, tiered by mass and destination, with a discount for African nationals and a surcharge for anyone who had ever signed an Exodus Solutions contract.",
      "You cannot argue with a price. You can argue with a warlord. You can send peacekeepers. You cannot send peacekeepers to a spreadsheet.",
      "Amara watched the story break on a monitor in the fabrication hall while Yuki ran the third truss-layer deposition behind her and didn't look up.",
      "\"He's going to run out of rockets,\" Amara said.",
      "\"He's going to run out of fuel first,\" Yuki said, still not looking up. \"The pad's fine. The pad's always been fine. There are eleven Soyuz-class airframes in storage at Site 31 and none of them can get to a transfer orbit without twelve hundred tonnes of kerolox that he doesn't have and can't make. He's selling something he can't deliver.\"",
      "Amara turned around slowly.",
      "\"How do you know what's in storage at Site 31?\"",
