      "The panel wasn't a panel. That was the first thing. Everyone imagined a solar array the way they imagined a sail — a flat thing catching light and passing it down a wire. The Helios design was a fan. Two hundred and forty mirrored facets on a folding spine, each one offset from the next by four-tenths of a degree, so that the whole structure could track a star through nine degrees of orbital drift without a single moving joint.",
      "That was elegant. Amara Okafor was elegant. Chen had spent two years hating her employer and admiring her, and the elegance was the problem.",
      "He did the arithmetic on paper, which was superstition, and then he did it on the terminal, which was not.",
      "Four-tenths of a degree, two hundred and forty facets, at the inclination Exodus had filed with four separate launch authorities. He drew the overlap. He redrew it with the spine at full deployment instead of ninety percent. He got an effective continuous sheet eleven hundred kilometres across at the L1 point, and a coverage figure of ninety-nine point four percent, and a shadow that was not a shadow cast by accident.",
      "He sat with it and tried to be wrong for six hours.",
      "At 1000 he found the margin note. It was in the spec, in the author's own hand, page four thousand and six, and it read: *retention at full span is asymmetric; hold for review.* It was dated eleven weeks before the first funding round closed.",
      "Somebody had known. Or somebody had half-known, and filed the half-knowledge as a comment, and gone on building, which in Chen's experience was worse.",
      "Then he found the second thing, and the second thing was the one that made his hands cold. Section 44. Safe mode. The array had no ground-command disassembly path. There was no uplink that would fold the spine. The only hardware capable of shuttering the facets was a control module in the same orbit, on the same truss, behind the same power bus, and the module's command keys had been provisioned by Exodus Solutions ninety days ago.",
      "You cannot argue with a control module.",
      "He wrote the post at 1100 and did not send it. A post was a manual. A manual in the open, this year, was a gift to Kwame Osei, who was selling launch seats at published rates, and to a man in a tower in Zurich who had already priced the species.",
      "He sent fourteen pages instead of forty. The flaw, the margin note, the orbit. Not the module. Not the keys.",
      "Isaiah Cross had it on air by 1400, and by 1500 he was saying the word *shade* in the same sentence as the word *Helios*, and by 1600 the feed was being jammed on three frequencies, which meant somebody had heard it and somebody had a budget.",
