      "The council does not vote on the expedition. Maya says she is going, and that is the vote.",
      "Kade packs his survey kit in the dark of C-8. He does not turn on the light. He has packed this kit forty-three times and he knows each item by weight: the thermal probe, the spare batteries, the laminated map that Eugene filed two years after the world ended and does not remember filing. He stands in the dark and listens to Lia moving in C-12, two doors down, and he does not call out to her because if he calls out she will answer, and if she answers he will hear that she is not afraid, and if he hears that she is not afraid he will have to decide whether to be afraid for her or for himself, and he is not ready to decide.",
      "Jin Alvarez is already in the ready room, sitting on the bench with his boots tied. He has drawn a grid on the wall in chalk, nine squares, and in seven of them he has written temperatures from the last seven surveys. The two empty squares wait for this trip. He looks at them for a long time before he stands up.",
